      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that generating a string of `1114111` code points (MAX_CODE_POINT) using a mocked `TextRandomProvider` that always returns `0` (an unassigned code point that gets skipped indefinitely) triggers an undeclared exception. I'll improve readability by renaming variables, adding a descriptive method name, and clarifying comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic EvoSuite-generated variable names (`randomStringGenerator_Builder0`, `textRandomProvider0`, `randomStringGenerator0`) with descriptive names (`builder`, `mockedRandom`, `generator`) and adds a Javadoc comment explaining why the mock's always-zero return causes an undeclared exception."
